      "message": "[info] Line 1261: `sock-\u003ewrite()` already calls `pimpl_-\u003eshutdown(ec)` internally when a transport write fails, so this extra `sock-\u003eshutdown()` is redundant for the common error path (it is idempotent, so harmless). It does add value for the pre-transport error cases (`isShutdown_`/`message_size`) where `write()` does not shut down — though tearing down the whole multiplexed socket on a `message_size` error would be heavy-handed. Given the 256-byte control buffer here that can\u0027t trigger, so this is fine as-is; a brief comment noting the intent would help.",
