      "side": 1,
      "message": "[info] Line 717: The success path now assumes `writeEndpoint` writes the full requested length whenever `!ec`, and increments `txBytes_` by the full sizes. TlsSocketEndpoint::write currently loops until fully written, so this holds today, but the returned `res` is inconsistent: for the one-shot path it is header+payload (`buffer.size()`), while for the multi-part path it is only the payload length (`len`), silently dropping the 16-byte header from the count. Since no caller depends on the exact return value on success this is not a bug, but returning the total bytes written (or asserting `res \u003d\u003d requested`) would make the contract clearer and guard against future short-write endpoints.",
      "revId": "5b6909b3140bbb3bb8b0a9467b5b41655dbadd46",
