      "side": 1,
      "message": "[info] Line 143: `ice_-\u003esend()` is a higher-level call and does not reliably set `errno` on failure, so `ec.assign(errno, std::generic_category())` may capture an unrelated/stale errno value. The `if (!ec) ec \u003d io_error;` fallback only covers the errno\u003d\u003d0 case, not a stale non-zero errno. Consider defaulting to `std::errc::io_error` unconditionally here (or documenting that errno is best-effort), since the caller only branches on `ec` being truthy anyway.",
      "revId": "5b6909b3140bbb3bb8b0a9467b5b41655dbadd46",
