      "side": 1,
      "message": "[warning] Line 2427: Asserting exactly `failedWrites \u003d\u003d 1` is racy. Once the injected callback fails a write, `MultiplexedSocket::write` calls `shutdown()`, so later writes short-circuit on the `isShutdown_` check before reaching the callback. However, the `isShutdown_` check in `write()` happens BEFORE `writeMtx` is taken, so a beacon/version write already running on the io_context can slip past that check concurrently with the channel-request write and hit the callback a second time, making `failedWrites \u003d\u003d 2`. Prefer `CPPUNIT_ASSERT(failedWrites.load() \u003e\u003d 1)` (the exact-count semantics aren\u0027t what the test is really verifying) to avoid intermittent CI failures.",
      "revId": "5b6909b3140bbb3bb8b0a9467b5b41655dbadd46",
